# =============================================================================
# Molaro et al. (2019) T = -20 C grain pair -- PRE-NECKED r = 14 um, dom2
#
# WHY NOT THE TANGENT START.
# The tangent geometries make the initial neck an OUTPUT, which is the right
# instinct, but they force the model to traverse r = 0 -> 16.4 um first, and
# that whole traverse is below its own resolution floor. Measured consequence
# (dom2 CFL ladder, 2026-08-19): a void opens at r ~ 5 um at t ~ 150-165 s,
# the ice seals over it, and it PERSISTS and DEEPENS (phi 0.69 -> 0.55 over
# 130 s) while the neck grows 7.8 -> 8.7 um. It is not a timestep artifact --
# a 20x tightening of -dtCFL_dphimax (0.20 -> 0.01) moved the trapped minimum
# only 0.498 -> 0.551.
#
# The cause is resolution, not time integration: at r = 5 um the fillet radius
# is rho = r^2/(2(R-r)) = 0.153 um = 0.59 eps at the old eps. The model was
# being asked to represent a feature THINNER THAN ITS OWN INTERFACE. Fixing
# that by refinement needs eps = 2.5e-8 -- 1044x the cost. Starting above the
# floor costs nothing.
#
# EPS = 1.18e-07, and two independent criteria pick it:
#   delta_ice < 1   requires eps <= 1.1802e-07   (thin-interface correction no
#                   longer exceeds the kinetic term it corrects; at the old
#                   2.5852e-07 with alpha_c = 0.1 it was delta_ice = 2.19)
#   start above the resolution floor requires eps <= r^2/(12 R) = 1.883e-07
# The first binds. Resulting numbers:
#   neck floor      sqrt(12 eps R) = 11.08 um
#   start r = 14 um is 1.26x above it; Molaro's first neck 16.4 um is 1.48x
#   fillet at r = 14 um: rho = 1.347 um = 11.4 eps  (needs >= 6)
#   delta_ice 1.000   delta_mean 0.158   delta_vap 0.067
#   tau_sub 1.332 s   mob_sub 2.9527e-08   alph_sub 4.7178e+08
#
# GEOMETRY. Centre separation solved analytically -- the union IC needs no
# calibration bisection, unlike the additive one:
#   d = sqrt(R0^2 - r^2) + sqrt(R1^2 - r^2) = 171.1604 um   (tangent is 173.5)
# Outside the union, sdf = min_k sdf_k is exact, and the occlusion correction
# only fires for sdf < 0, so the phi = 0.5 contour IS the sharp union surface.
# Verified numerically: measured waist 14.05 um at this eps (+0.4 %), and the
# residual shrinks with eps -- so no preprocess/calibrate_neck_geometry.py run
# is needed (that tool targets the ADDITIVE IC, which does need it).
#
# Neck plane sits at z = c0 + sqrt(R0^2 - r^2) = 196.305 um.
#
# Measure with: python postprocess/neck_width.py <run_dir> --axisym
#               python postprocess/grain_shrinkage.py <run_dir>
# Anchor + fit: python postprocess/fit_neck_growth.py <run>/neck_width.csv \
#                   inputs/validation/molaro2019_fig11_T-20.csv \
#                   --anchor-neck 1.6405e-5 --demmenie
# =============================================================================

-axisym 1
-ic_grain_union 1                       # phi=0.5 lands on the sharp union
                                        # surface for ANY eps; the additive
                                        # default would need per-eps calibration

-ic_type multi_grains
-dim 2
-Lx 4.50000e-04
-Ly 2.25000e-04
-Lz 0

-ice_grain_cx 1.251698e-04,2.963302e-04   # d = 1.711604e-04 -> neck r = 14 um
-ice_grain_cy 0.0,0.0                   # grains on the axisymmetric axis
-ice_grain_R  7.25e-5,1.01e-4
-ice_grain_ax 7.25e-5,1.01e-4
-ice_grain_ay 7.25e-5,1.01e-4

-Nx 5394                                # h = eps/sqrt(2) = 8.3439e-08
-Ny 2697                                # (14.55M elements, 43.7M DoF)
-Nz 1
-eps 1.1800e-07
-eps_valid_temp -20

-delt_t 1.0e-4
-periodic 0
